window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-1716f9f1a07bca7e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-cli-quickstart\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security-cli\">Codex Security CLI 快速入门</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用独立的 Codex Security CLI 对本地代码仓库执行标准扫描。本快速入门会生成一份可供查看和日后回顾的报告。如果要在 Codex 对话中扫描，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security 插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"check-the-prerequisites\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">检查前置条件</h2> <p>你需要 Node.js 24 或 26，或 Node.js 22 系列中不低于 22.13.0 的版本。还需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本。Python 3.10 还需要 <code>tomli</code>。使用 OpenAI 推理进行扫描需要具备 Codex Security 访问权限。根据你的账户和代码仓库，执行全仓库扫描还可能需要<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">网络安全可信访问权限（Trusted Access for Cyber）（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>CLI 会使用你当前操作系统账户的权限运行，也不会暂停等待审批。扫描进程可能继承当前环境变量；开始前请移除与任务无关的凭据。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=local-scan-permissions\">本地扫描权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-and-verify-the-cli\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"cli\">设置并验证 CLI</h2> <p>通过 <code>npx</code> 运行公开发布的软件包：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security --version\n</code></pre> <p>该命令会显示已安装的软件包版本。使用 <code>info --json</code> 检查打包的插件版本，或使用 <code>--help</code> 查看命令列表。软件包变更记录见 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI 和 SDK 版本发布记录（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"sign-in\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">登录</h2> <p>使用 ChatGPT 账户登录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security login\n</code></pre> <p>如果当前机器没有浏览器，请添加 <code>--device-auth</code>，并按照显示的登录说明操作。即使你的环境中也存在 API 密钥，仍可在下方扫描命令中使用 <code>--auth chatgpt</code> 明确选择 ChatGPT 登录方式。</p> <p>有关 API 密钥和其他提供方，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-scan-authentication\">选择扫描身份验证方式</a>。要使用 Amazon Bedrock，请配置 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-amazon-bedrock\">AWS 凭据和模型访问权限</a>，而不是使用 ChatGPT 登录或 OpenAI API 密钥。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-a-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">准备扫描</h2> <p>将以下路径替换为你的代码仓库路径，以及一个位于该 Git 工作树之外的新结果目录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">REPOSITORY=/path/to/repository\nSCAN_DIR=/path/outside/repository/codex-security-results\n</code></pre> <p>扫描结果可能包含源代码摘录和漏洞详情。请将结果保存到私密位置。如果省略 <code>--output-dir</code>，CLI 会使用其持久状态目录。</p> <p>检查目标路径和输出位置：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan \"$REPOSITORY\" \\\n  --auth chatgpt --output-dir \"$SCAN_DIR\" --dry-run\n</code></pre> <p>试运行成功只能确认本地输入有效。它不会启动扫描、加载凭据，也不会检查插件的 Python 解释器，因此不能证明身份验证和运行时设置一定可以成功。</p> <p><a id=\"run-your-first-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">执行首次扫描</h2> <p>删除 <code>--dry-run</code> 以开始扫描：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan \"$REPOSITORY\" \\\n  --auth chatgpt --output-dir \"$SCAN_DIR\"\n</code></pre> <p>交互式终端会显示实时仪表板；非交互式终端会显示进度行。即使在交互式终端中，也可以添加 <code>--headless</code> 改为使用进度行。仪表板和已保存日志可能包含源代码或凭据；分享之前请先检查。</p> <p>扫描结束后，标准错误输出中会包含报告路径、发现项数量和耗时。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">  REPORT    /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results/report.md\n\n  FINDINGS  2 (2 confirmed this scan; 0 previously found; 1 high, 1 medium)\n  ELAPSED   42s\n  RESULTS   /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">报告      /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results/report.md\n\n  发现项    2（本次扫描确认 2 项；此前发现 0 项；高严重级别 1 项，中严重级别 1 项）\n  耗时      42s\n  结果      /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results</div></div> <p>默认情况下，发现项的严重级别不会导致扫描失败。若要让标准输出采用机器可读格式，请添加 <code>--json</code>。若要让发现项导致 CI 检查失败，请设置<a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">严重级别策略</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">查看结果</h2> <p>打开报告目录中的 <code>report.md</code>。先确认扫描目标和代码修订版本，再查看覆盖情况，然后逐项检查发现项。</p> <p>查看 <code>scan-manifest.json</code> 中的 <code>scan.status</code>，确认扫描已完成。查看 <code>coverage.json</code> 中已检查的范围、排除路径、延后处理的工作和待解决问题。</p> <p>扫描完成后通常以退出码 <code>0</code> 结束；如果发现项达到已配置的严重级别阈值，则返回 <code>1</code>。覆盖缺口不会改变退出码，因此退出码 <code>0</code> 并不表示所有文件都已审核。输入、执行、结果完整性或必要输出失败时会返回 <code>2</code>。有关退出码的说明，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">CLI 参考</a>。</p> <p>对于每项发现，请检查受影响的代码、攻击者所需前提、验证证据和仍未排除的不确定性。基于源代码分析得出的发现不一定包含成功的运行时复现证据。只有证据足以支持所声称的问题时，才应选择该发现进行修复。</p> <p>分享或归档扫描结果时，请保留完整的扫描目录。目录中包含 <code>scan-manifest.json</code>、<code>findings.json</code> 和 <code>coverage.json</code>，以及报告和支持材料。完整目录结构请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=scan-artifacts\">扫描产物</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"revisit-a-saved-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">重新查看已保存的扫描</h2> <p>列出该代码仓库的扫描记录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans list \"$REPOSITORY\"\n</code></pre> <p>从结果中复制一个扫描 ID：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>交互式扫描完成且发现了问题时，CLI 还会提供发现项浏览器。在选择修复方案之前，请先在其中查看证据。若要查看已保存的发现项，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-validate-and-codex-security-patch\">验证和补丁命令</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-next-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">选择下一步扫描</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>目标</th> <th>指南</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>扫描选定路径或差异内容</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-the-scan-target\">选择扫描目标</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用深度扫描或限制其运行时间</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\">配置深度扫描</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>提供架构或安全策略</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=add-security-context\">添加安全上下文</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>更改模型或推理强度</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-the-runtime\">配置运行时</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>设置预估费用上限</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=set-output-and-policy-options\">输出和策略选项</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>扫描多个代码仓库</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">批量扫描</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>扫描 GitHub 拉取请求或安排定期扫描</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">GitHub Actions 指南</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>选择其他 CI 提供商</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD 概览</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>有关身份验证问题、重复扫描结果差异或误报反馈，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-d4672d2ba61dcd68\">CLI 常见问题</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-cli-quickstart\">Codex Security CLI quickstart</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Run a standard scan of a local repository with the standalone Codex Security CLI. This quickstart ends with a saved report you can review and revisit. For scans inside a Codex conversation, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security plugin</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"check-the-prerequisites\">Check the prerequisites</h2> <p>Use Node.js 24 or 26, or Node.js 22 starting with 22.13.0. You also need Python 3.10 or later. Python 3.10 also needs <code>tomli</code>. Scans using OpenAI inference require Codex Security access. Depending on your account and repository, full-repository scans may also require <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trusted Access for Cyber (online)</a>.</p> <p>The CLI runs with your operating-system permissions and doesn't pause for approval. Scan processes can inherit your environment, so remove unrelated credentials before starting. See <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=local-scan-permissions\">Local scan permissions</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-and-verify-the-cli\">Set up and verify the CLI</h2> <p>Run the public package with <code>npx</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security --version\n</code></pre> <p>The command prints the installed package version. Use <code>info --json</code> to check the bundled plugin version, or <code>--help</code> to list commands. Package changes are listed in the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI and SDK releases (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"sign-in\">Sign in</h2> <p>Sign in with your ChatGPT account:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security login\n</code></pre> <p>On a machine without a browser, add <code>--device-auth</code> and follow the displayed sign-in instructions. Use <code>--auth chatgpt</code> in the scan commands below to select that sign-in even when your environment also contains an API key.</p> <p>For API keys and other providers, see <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-scan-authentication\">Select scan authentication</a>. For Amazon Bedrock, use <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-amazon-bedrock\">AWS credentials and model access</a> instead of a ChatGPT sign-in or OpenAI API key.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-a-scan\">Prepare a scan</h2> <p>Replace these paths with your repository and a new results directory outside its Git worktree:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">REPOSITORY=/path/to/repository\nSCAN_DIR=/path/outside/repository/codex-security-results\n</code></pre> <p>Results can include source excerpts and vulnerability details. Choose a private location. If you omit <code>--output-dir</code>, the CLI uses its persistent state directory.</p> <p>Check the target and output location:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan \"$REPOSITORY\" \\\n  --auth chatgpt --output-dir \"$SCAN_DIR\" --dry-run\n</code></pre> <p>A successful dry run confirms the local inputs. It doesn't start a scan, load credentials, or check the plugin's Python interpreter, so it doesn't establish that authentication and runtime setup will succeed.</p> <h2 id=\"run-your-first-scan\">Run your first scan</h2> <p>Remove <code>--dry-run</code> to start the scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scan \"$REPOSITORY\" \\\n  --auth chatgpt --output-dir \"$SCAN_DIR\"\n</code></pre> <p>An interactive terminal shows a live dashboard. Non-interactive terminals show progress lines. Add <code>--headless</code> to use progress lines in an interactive terminal too. The dashboard and saved logs can contain source code or credentials. Review them before sharing.</p> <p>When the scan finishes, stderr includes the report path, finding count, and elapsed time. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">  REPORT    /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results/report.md\n\n  FINDINGS  2 (2 confirmed this scan; 0 previously found; 1 high, 1 medium)\n  ELAPSED   42s\n  RESULTS   /path/outside/repository/codex-security-results\n</code></pre> <p>By default, the severity of a finding doesn't cause a scan to fail. For machine-readable stdout, add <code>--json</code>. To make findings fail a CI check, set a <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">severity policy</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-results\">Review the results</h2> <p>Open <code>report.md</code> from the reported directory. Confirm the target and revision, then read the coverage before reviewing individual findings.</p> <p>Check <code>scan.status</code> in <code>scan-manifest.json</code> to confirm that the scan completed. Review <code>coverage.json</code> for reviewed surfaces, excluded paths, deferred work, and open questions.</p> <p>A completed scan exits with <code>0</code> unless findings meet a configured severity threshold, which returns <code>1</code>. Coverage gaps don't change the exit code, so exit <code>0</code> doesn't mean every file was reviewed. Input, execution, result-integrity, or required-output failures return <code>2</code>. The <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">CLI reference</a> explains the exit codes.</p> <p>For each finding, check the affected code, attacker prerequisites, validation evidence, and remaining uncertainty. A source-based finding doesn't necessarily include a successful runtime reproduction. Select a finding for remediation only after its evidence supports the claimed issue.</p> <p>Keep the scan directory together when sharing or archiving it. It contains <code>scan-manifest.json</code>, <code>findings.json</code>, and <code>coverage.json</code> alongside the report and supporting artifacts. See <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=scan-artifacts\">Scan artifacts</a> for the full layout.</p> <h2 id=\"revisit-a-saved-scan\">Revisit a saved scan</h2> <p>List scans for the repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans list \"$REPOSITORY\"\n</code></pre> <p>Copy a scan ID from the results:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security scans show SCAN_ID\n</code></pre> <p>After a complete interactive scan with findings, the CLI also offers a finding browser. Review the evidence there before choosing a fix. For saved findings, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-validate-and-codex-security-patch\">validate and patch commands</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-next-scan\">Choose the next scan</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Goal</th> <th>Guide</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Scan selected paths or a diff</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=select-the-scan-target\">Select the scan target</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use deep scans or limit their runtime</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\">Configure deep scans</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Supply architecture or security policies</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=add-security-context\">Add security context</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Change the model or reasoning effort</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-the-runtime\">Configure the runtime</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Set an estimated cost limit</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=set-output-and-policy-options\">Output and policy options</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scan multiple repositories</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">Bulk scans</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scan GitHub pull requests or run scheduled scans</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cb94fa07f6e7450c\">GitHub Actions guide</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Choose another CI provider</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">CI/CD overview</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For authentication problems, repeat-scan differences, or false-positive feedback, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-d4672d2ba61dcd68\">CLI FAQ</a>.</p>"};
